7
00:01:15.572 --> 00:01:18.681
ELECTRIC GUITAR PLAYS
BEETHOVEN'S FIFTH SYMPHONY

8
00:01:20.901 --> 00:01:23.251
SHE CLEARS HER THROAT

9
00:01:26.417 --> 00:01:28.064
GUITAR FEEDBACK

10
00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:37.672
- Potts?
- Yeah.

11
00:01:37.867 --> 00:01:39.409
Bill Potts.

12
00:01:39.578 --> 00:01:40.976
You wanted to see me.

13
00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:43.390
Er. you're not a student
at this university.

14
00:01:43.578 --> 00:01:46.138
- No. I work in the canteen.
- Yeah. but you come to my lectures.

15
00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:49.094
No. I don't. I never do that.

16
00:01:49.219 --> 00:01:50.437
I've seen you.

17
00:01:50.555 --> 00:01:53.523
Love your lectures.
They're totally awesome.

18
00:01:53.648 --> 00:01:55.624
Why d'you come to my lectures
when you're not a student?

19
00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:58.047
OK. so my first day
here. in the canteen.

20
00:01:58.109 --> 00:02:01.484
I was on chips. There was this girl.
Student. Beautiful.

21
00:02:01.609 --> 00:02:04.218
Like a model. only with
talking and thinking.

22
00:02:04.406 --> 00:02:08.750
She looked at you and you perved.
Every time. automatic. Like physics.

23
00:02:08.914 --> 00:02:12.633
Eye contact. perversion.
So I gave her extra chips.

24
00:02:12.992 --> 00:02:16.093
Every time. extra chips. Like a
reward for all the perversion.

25
00:02:16.242 --> 00:02:19.148
Every day. got myself
on chips. rewarded her.

26
00:02:19.297 --> 00:02:22.109
Then. finally. finally.
she looked at me.

27
00:02:22.281 --> 00:02:25.883
Like she'd noticed. actually
noticed. all the extra chips.

28
00:02:26.054 --> 00:02:27.489
Do you know what I realised?

29
00:02:27.888 --> 00:02:29.343
She was fat.

30
00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.625
I'd fatted her.

31
00:02:33.437 --> 00:02:36.468
But that's life. isn't it?
Beauty or chips. I like chips.

32
00:02:36.586 --> 00:02:39.062
So did she. So that's OK.

33
00:02:39.664 --> 00:02:41.804
And how does that in any way explain

34
00:02:41.906 --> 00:02:43.992
why you keep coming to my lectures?

35
00:02:44.109 --> 00:02:47.898
Yeah. it doesn't really. does it? I
was hoping something would develop.

36
00:02:48.031 --> 00:02:49.889
What's that?

37
00:02:50.163 --> 00:02:51.643
A police telephone box?

38
00:02:52.875 --> 00:02:55.531
- Yeah.
- Did you build it from a kit?

39
00:02:55.695 --> 00:02:58.015
- No. it came like that.
- Then how did you get it in here?

40
00:02:58.086 --> 00:03:00.000
The door's too small and
so are the windows.

41
00:03:00.101 --> 00:03:03.265
I had the window and a part of the
wall taken out and it was lifted in.

42
00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:06.769
- What. with a crane?
- Yeah. with a crane.

43
00:03:06.867 --> 00:03:08.049
It's heavier than it looks.

44
00:03:08.109 --> 00:03:11.369
- Why do you keep coming to my lectures?
- Because I like them.

45
00:03:11.625 --> 00:03:14.422
Everybody likes them. they're amazing.

46
00:03:15.336 --> 00:03:17.117
- Why me?
- Why you what?

47
00:03:17.211 --> 00:03:19.105
Plenty of people come to your
lectures that aren't supposed to.

48
00:03:19.129 --> 00:03:21.859
- Why pick on me?
- Well. I noticed you.

49
00:03:22.019 --> 00:03:24.011
Yeah. but why?

50
00:03:25.539 --> 00:03:28.086
Well. most people when don't
understand something. they frown.

51
00:03:28.198 --> 00:03:29.601
You...

52
00:03:30.428 --> 00:03:31.708
..smile.

53
00:03:33.898 --> 00:03:35.640
I'll tell you what I don't understand.

54
00:03:35.773 --> 00:03:38.984
You've been lecturing here
for a long time. 50 years.

55
00:03:39.078 --> 00:03:40.211
some people say.

56
00:03:40.303 --> 00:03:42.116
Nabeela in the office says over 70.

57
00:03:42.195 --> 00:03:44.491
Yeah. And you're thinking. "Well.
he doesn't look old enough"?

58
00:03:44.515 --> 00:03:47.515
No. I'm wondering what you're
supposed to be lecturing on.

59
00:03:47.633 --> 00:03:50.484
It's like the university let
you do whatever you like.

60
00:03:50.656 --> 00:03:53.304
One time. you were going to give
a lecture on quantum physics.

61
00:03:53.406 --> 00:03:56.054
- You talked about poetry.
- Poetry. physics. same thing.

62
00:03:56.156 --> 00:03:57.578
How is it the same?

63
00:03:57.655 --> 00:04:00.023
Because of the rhymes. What are
you doing at this university?

64
00:04:00.047 --> 00:04:02.976
- I always wanted to come here.
- Yeah. to serve chips?

65
00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:06.570
So anyway. am I nearly done?

66
00:04:06.734 --> 00:04:07.922
Do you want to be?

67
00:04:08.153 --> 00:04:09.433
See ya.

68
00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:14.052
You ever get less than a
first. then it's over.

69
00:04:14.538 --> 00:04:16.147
- You what?
- A first.

70
00:04:16.819 --> 00:04:20.115
- Every time. or I stop immediately.
- Stop what?

71
00:04:20.209 --> 00:04:21.998
Being your personal tutor.

72
00:04:23.545 --> 00:04:25.609
But I'm not a student.

73
00:04:25.927 --> 00:04:27.444
I'm not part of the university.

74
00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:29.186
I never even applied.

75
00:04:29.358 --> 00:04:30.748
We'll sort all that out later.

76
00:04:30.857 --> 00:04:32.545
You kind of have to
sort that out earlier.

77
00:04:32.694 --> 00:04:35.061
Leave it with me. I'm
assuming that it's a yes.

78
00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:39.483
- Yes.
- I'll see you at 6pm every weekday.

79
00:04:39.569 --> 00:04:41.701
I don't care who's dying
never. ever be late.

80
00:04:41.772 --> 00:04:43.975
I'm very particular about time.

81
00:04:46.743 --> 00:04:48.076
Oh. um...

82
00:04:49.549 --> 00:04:51.764
People just call you the Doctor?

83
00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:54.139
What do I call you?

84
00:04:54.303 --> 00:04:55.662
The Doctor.

85
00:04:55.843 --> 00:04:59.897
But Doctor's not a name.
 I can't just call you Doctor.

86
00:05:01.278 --> 00:05:02.638
Doctor what?

87
00:05:27.841 --> 00:05:31.146
<font color=#FF00FF>*DOCTOR WHO*</font>
<font color=#00FF00>Season 10 Episode 01</font>

88
00:05:36.754 --> 00:05:40.387
<font color=#FFFF00>"The Pilot"</font>

89
00:05:41.225 --> 00:05:42.724
RHTHYMIC BEEPING

90
00:05:46.959 --> 00:05:49.201
Time! Time doesn't pass.

91
00:05:49.467 --> 00:05:53.655
The passage of time is an illusion.
and life is the magician.

92
00:05:55.514 --> 00:05:59.272
Because life only lets you
see one day at a time.

93
00:06:04.209 --> 00:06:05.725
You remember being alive yesterday.

94
00:06:05.795 --> 00:06:07.506
you hope you're going
to be alive tomorrow.

95
00:06:07.576 --> 00:06:11.428
So it feels like you're
travelling from one to the other.

96
00:06:11.483 --> 00:06:13.756
But nobody's moving anywhere.

97
00:06:13.982 --> 00:06:16.764
- Movies don't really move.
- BELL CHIMES

98
00:06:16.983 --> 00:06:19.426
They're just pictures.
lots and lots of pictures.

99
00:06:19.590 --> 00:06:23.074
All of them still. none of them moving.
Just frozen moments.

100
00:06:23.203 --> 00:06:24.770
BELL CONTINUES TO CHIME

101
00:06:26.465 --> 00:06:30.425
But if you experience those
pictures one after the other.

102
00:06:30.582 --> 00:06:32.801
then everything comes alive.

103
00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:39.926
- Am I on time?
- That's a very big question.

104
00:06:46.332 --> 00:06:48.590
You know you're my foster mum?

105
00:06:48.824 --> 00:06:50.527
He's like my foster tutor.

106
00:06:50.715 --> 00:06:53.238
Am I going to have to break
every bone in his body?

107
00:06:53.387 --> 00:06:54.848
It's not like that.

108
00:06:54.947 --> 00:06:56.871
You need to keep your eye on men.

109
00:06:58.863 --> 00:07:01.059
Men aren't where I
keep my eye. actually.

110
00:07:01.137 --> 00:07:03.543
Imagine if time all happened at once...

111
00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:10.270
..every moment of your life
laid out around you...

112
00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:15.809
..like a city. Streets full
of buildings made of days.

113
00:07:15.934 --> 00:07:19.105
The day you were born. the day you die.

114
00:07:19.191 --> 00:07:22.238
The day you fall in love.
the day that love ends.

115
00:07:22.339 --> 00:07:27.473
A whole city built from triumph
and heartbreak and boredom

116
00:07:27.527 --> 00:07:30.254
and laughter and cutting your toenails.

117
00:07:30.316 --> 00:07:32.551
It's the best place you will ever be.

118
00:07:32.637 --> 00:07:34.449
MUSIC AND LAUGHTER

119
00:07:35.668 --> 00:07:40.290
Time is a structure
relative to ourselves.

120
00:07:44.186 --> 00:07:45.425
I'll get them in.

121
00:07:45.581 --> 00:07:49.473
Time is the space made by our lives

122
00:07:49.566 --> 00:07:54.215
where we stand together. forever.

123
00:07:54.762 --> 00:07:58.582
Time And Relative Dimension...

124
00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:01.504
..in Space.

125
00:08:04.707 --> 00:08:06.209
It means life.

126
00:08:06.434 --> 00:08:08.582
RHYTHMIC BEEPING

127
00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:11.074
- Just chips. yeah?
- Please.

128
00:08:29.775 --> 00:08:31.291
Ooh!

129
00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:47.571
HANDLE CLANKS

130
00:08:48.288 --> 00:08:49.798
METALLIC SCRAPING

131
00:09:03.759 --> 00:09:06.689
So you're tutoring her. then?

132
00:09:07.370 --> 00:09:09.769
- Yes. I am.
- Why?

133
00:09:10.001 --> 00:09:11.209
Why not?

134
00:09:11.314 --> 00:09:13.259
You're not supposed to get involved.

135
00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:16.001
What are you teaching her anyway?

136
00:09:16.090 --> 00:09:17.449
Everything.

137
00:09:17.712 --> 00:09:19.649
Well. how can you teach
anyone everything?

138
00:09:19.736 --> 00:09:21.290
Because everything rhymes.

139
00:09:23.210 --> 00:09:28.369
Links apple and alpha.
synchronous and diverging...

140
00:09:28.844 --> 00:09:29.912
BEEPING

141
00:09:30.033 --> 00:09:31.236
Yeah. you want to turn that.

142
00:09:31.356 --> 00:09:32.996
BEEPING CONTINUES

143
00:09:34.492 --> 00:09:36.172
You want to rotate it.

144
00:09:40.564 --> 00:09:42.324
CLATTERING

145
00:09:49.008 --> 00:09:51.489
The door upstairs. how did
you set the security?

146
00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:53.375
Friends only.

147
00:09:56.927 --> 00:09:58.770
BEEPING

148
00:09:59.997 --> 00:10:02.270
So turn it. and then it'll...

149
00:10:02.638 --> 00:10:04.599
- I'm turning it.
- All right.

150
00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:34.130
- You OK?
- Yeah. I'm fine.

151
00:10:39.021 --> 00:10:41.506
Sorry. can I ask what's
that in your eye?

152
00:10:41.654 --> 00:10:43.904
It's just a defect in the iris.

153
00:10:44.014 --> 00:10:46.092
- Looks like a star.
- Well. it's a defect.

154
00:10:46.153 --> 00:10:47.783
At least it's a defect
that looks like a star.

155
00:10:47.807 --> 00:10:49.264
I'm getting it fixed.

156
00:10:51.122 --> 00:10:52.562
OK.

157
00:10:55.212 --> 00:10:59.798
Sorry. None of my business. but are
you freaking out about something?

158
00:11:04.089 --> 00:11:07.609
Please. You can say no.
Would you come with me?

159
00:11:07.815 --> 00:11:09.190
Can I show you something?

160
00:11:09.352 --> 00:11:10.672
God. yes.

161
00:11:12.769 --> 00:11:15.722
- I love this place. don't you?
- Hate it.

162
00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:18.519
- Why?
- I don't know. I just do.

163
00:11:18.956 --> 00:11:21.449
Everywhere I go I just want to leave.

164
00:11:21.723 --> 00:11:23.120
Can I come too?

165
00:11:24.452 --> 00:11:25.772
Maybe.

166
00:11:38.007 --> 00:11:39.865
There's a puddle over there.

167
00:11:40.163 --> 00:11:42.061
But it hasn't rained for a week.

168
00:11:42.280 --> 00:11:45.694
Yeah. but. well. you know. half
the students here are blokes...

169
00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:47.288
Go and look in it.

170
00:11:47.428 --> 00:11:49.788
- You want me to look in a puddle?
- Please.

171
00:11:58.224 --> 00:11:59.710
OK. I'm looking.

172
00:12:00.929 --> 00:12:03.329
- What am I looking at?
- Your reflection.

173
00:12:05.585 --> 00:12:08.538
- Yep. There it is.
- Do you see what's wrong with it?

174
00:12:08.616 --> 00:12:10.811
My name's Bill. by the way.

175
00:12:10.898 --> 00:12:12.327
Heather.

176
00:12:12.593 --> 00:12:14.289
Can you see what's wrong?

177
00:12:14.454 --> 00:12:16.436
Nothing. It just looks like me.

178
00:12:18.552 --> 00:12:19.911
Oh!

179
00:12:20.069 --> 00:12:21.569
What is that?

180
00:12:23.373 --> 00:12:25.522
That's me. that's my face. but...

181
00:12:26.237 --> 00:12:28.117
It's wrong.

182
00:12:29.655 --> 00:12:33.171
- Hey!
- Sorry. Some other time.

183
00:12:34.675 --> 00:12:36.035
Promise?

184
00:12:40.532 --> 00:12:43.132
Pilot is located.

185
00:12:44.771 --> 00:12:48.170
Link is established.

186
00:12:48.701 --> 00:12:53.084
CHOIR SINGS JINGLE BELLS

187
00:12:53.228 --> 00:12:54.521
BELL CHIMES

188
00:13:08.475 --> 00:13:10.649
It's a rug.

189
00:13:10.999 --> 00:13:12.529
Haven't got you anything.

190
00:13:12.896 --> 00:13:15.092
It's OK. it was cheap.

191
00:13:17.788 --> 00:13:21.460
♪ Oh. what fun it is to ride in
a one-horse open sleigh... ♪

192
00:13:23.038 --> 00:13:24.967
Going anywhere for Christmas?

193
00:13:25.092 --> 00:13:26.368
I never go anywhere.

194
00:13:26.431 --> 00:13:28.150
That's not true.

195
00:13:28.249 --> 00:13:29.780
You go places. I can tell.

196
00:13:30.028 --> 00:13:31.427
My mum always said.

197
00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:33.780
"With some people you can smell
the wind in their clothes."

198
00:13:34.124 --> 00:13:35.403
Oh.

199
00:13:35.593 --> 00:13:38.843
She sounds... nice.

200
00:13:39.593 --> 00:13:41.049
She died when I was a baby.

201
00:13:41.194 --> 00:13:43.210
- Oh.
- Yeah.

202
00:13:46.365 --> 00:13:49.670
If she died when you were a
baby. when did she say that?

203
00:13:49.965 --> 00:13:51.365
In my head.

204
00:13:53.357 --> 00:13:56.630
I'm supposed to look like
her. but I don't really know.

205
00:13:57.123 --> 00:13:59.170
There's hardly any photographs.

206
00:13:59.378 --> 00:14:01.458
She hated having her picture taken.

207
00:14:02.591 --> 00:14:06.263
But if someone's gone.
do pictures really help?

208
00:14:09.716 --> 00:14:12.466
I thought you'd enjoy choosing
something for yourself.

209
00:14:12.591 --> 00:14:15.037
as you're always passing judgments.

210
00:14:16.427 --> 00:14:18.537
I hope you didn't spend
too much on this.

211
00:14:18.654 --> 00:14:20.623
Nah. This should cover it.

212
00:14:20.779 --> 00:14:22.089
What's that?

213
00:14:22.209 --> 00:14:24.318
Ooh. I found that at the
back of the cupboard

214
00:14:24.357 --> 00:14:28.005
with all your old stuff.
Just photographs of your mum.

215
00:14:28.561 --> 00:14:30.121
I didn't know we had 'em.

216
00:14:49.381 --> 00:14:50.421
SHE SNIFFS

217
00:15:16.490 --> 00:15:18.049
DOOR OPENS. CREAKS

218
00:15:18.114 --> 00:15:19.560
Happy new term!

219
00:15:19.966 --> 00:15:21.566
With you in a moment.

220
00:15:26.921 --> 00:15:29.163
You said you needed a
crane to lift your box.

221
00:15:29.290 --> 00:15:30.930
Sorry. what did you say?

222
00:15:58.465 --> 00:15:59.745
Hey!

223
00:16:02.374 --> 00:16:04.094
Still making eyes at a puddle?

224
00:16:05.507 --> 00:16:08.184
Did you ever work out what was
wrong with your reflection?

225
00:16:08.273 --> 00:16:09.539
Nah.

226
00:16:09.872 --> 00:16:12.117
Come round. I'll show you.

227
00:16:12.838 --> 00:16:14.367
Promise you won't go?

228
00:16:15.444 --> 00:16:16.764
Promise.

229
00:16:37.289 --> 00:16:38.547
OK.

230
00:16:38.825 --> 00:16:40.425
Yeah. no worries.

231
00:16:42.690 --> 00:16:47.268
Pilot confirmed.
Pilot engaged.

232
00:16:50.802 --> 00:16:52.560
DOOR CREAKS SHUT

233
00:16:57.249 --> 00:16:58.609
What's wrong?

234
00:17:00.616 --> 00:17:04.022
She said it was a defect.
but what kind of defect

235
00:17:04.081 --> 00:17:05.772
puts a star in your eye?

236
00:17:06.483 --> 00:17:09.600
But that doesn't even matter
because she was right.

237
00:17:10.155 --> 00:17:12.764
There was something wrong when
you looked in the puddle.

238
00:17:13.866 --> 00:17:17.499
That was definitely my face.
I see my face all the time.

239
00:17:17.694 --> 00:17:19.733
I've never liked it.
it's all over the place.

240
00:17:19.811 --> 00:17:22.217
It's always doing expressions
when I'm trying to be enigmatic.

241
00:17:22.241 --> 00:17:23.960
I know my face.

242
00:17:24.241 --> 00:17:27.066
and there was something wrong
with my face in the puddle.

243
00:17:28.758 --> 00:17:30.958
What could be wrong with your own face?

244
00:17:43.470 --> 00:17:44.931
Doctor!

245
00:17:49.646 --> 00:17:51.326
Doctor!

246
00:18:00.380 --> 00:18:02.137
- Why do you run like that?
- Like what?

247
00:18:02.262 --> 00:18:04.450
Like a penguin
with its arse on fire.

248
00:18:04.704 --> 00:18:06.064
Ergonomics.

249
00:18:06.739 --> 00:18:08.255
That's my face. yeah?

250
00:18:08.450 --> 00:18:10.010
You seem a bit
flexible on the subject.

251
00:18:10.034 --> 00:18:11.529
Oh. you've no idea.

252
00:18:11.692 --> 00:18:13.404
Maybe it's got to do with
that thing in her eye.

253
00:18:13.428 --> 00:18:14.461
How?

254
00:18:14.497 --> 00:18:16.622
Maybe she's like...
affected by something.

255
00:18:16.718 --> 00:18:17.739
Like what?

256
00:18:17.809 --> 00:18:20.465
I don't know. Look. I know you
know lots of stuff about.

257
00:18:20.590 --> 00:18:23.489
well. basically everything.
but do you know any sci-fi?

258
00:18:28.903 --> 00:18:30.067
Go on.

259
00:18:30.153 --> 00:18:33.239
Well. what if she's... possessed.

260
00:18:33.473 --> 00:18:34.926
Something like that.

261
00:18:35.176 --> 00:18:36.442
Possessed by what?

262
00:18:36.518 --> 00:18:38.317
I don't know.

263
00:18:38.762 --> 00:18:42.387
I saw this thing on Netflix.
Lizards in people's brains.

264
00:18:42.895 --> 00:18:45.286
Right. So. you meet a girl
with a discoloured iris

265
00:18:45.340 --> 00:18:48.364
and your first thought is she
might have a lizard in her brain?

266
00:18:48.708 --> 00:18:50.755
I can see I'm going to
have to up my game.

267
00:18:53.762 --> 00:18:55.715
- Oh...
- What?

268
00:18:55.778 --> 00:18:56.801
Oh!

269
00:18:56.848 --> 00:19:00.356
- What is it. what?
- Oh. I get it. I see it.

270
00:19:00.872 --> 00:19:03.520
It was easy for your
friend because of her eye.

271
00:19:03.637 --> 00:19:05.169
Because it gives her
special powers?

272
00:19:05.215 --> 00:19:09.020
No! Because her face
isn't symmetrical. Look!

273
00:19:10.572 --> 00:19:12.309
Look into the puddle.

274
00:19:13.067 --> 00:19:16.473
Your face looks wrong.
because it looks right.

275
00:19:16.669 --> 00:19:19.481
What's the one thing you never see
when you look in a reflection?

276
00:19:19.676 --> 00:19:23.270
Your face. You never see your
face the right way round.

277
00:19:24.239 --> 00:19:27.083
Right. Look for a freckle
or a funny tooth.

278
00:19:27.176 --> 00:19:29.075
- Something that's not symmetrical.
- My badge!

279
00:19:29.200 --> 00:19:32.153
See. your friend saw it
straightaway because of her eye.

280
00:19:32.715 --> 00:19:35.610
But... it's moving like a reflection.

281
00:19:42.685 --> 00:19:45.575
It's not reflecting you.

282
00:19:45.667 --> 00:19:47.107
It's mimicking you.

283
00:19:48.583 --> 00:19:51.169
There's something in the
water pretending to be you.

284
00:19:53.442 --> 00:19:57.169
Of course. it isn't water.

285
00:19:58.410 --> 00:20:00.848
Now what are these?
Let's have a look.

286
00:20:01.458 --> 00:20:02.738
What are they?

287
00:20:03.735 --> 00:20:05.255
Scorch marks.

288
00:20:06.011 --> 00:20:07.251
Interesting.

289
00:20:14.204 --> 00:20:15.404
Right. you.

290
00:20:17.728 --> 00:20:19.666
- Let's get you on the bus!
- The what. the bus?

291
00:20:19.744 --> 00:20:21.569
Tutorial's over.
take the night off.

292
00:20:21.736 --> 00:20:24.369
It's all cancelled. Go
and be a proper student

293
00:20:24.486 --> 00:20:26.752
texts. snogging. a vegan wrap.

294
00:20:26.877 --> 00:20:28.289
But what about the puddle?

295
00:20:28.392 --> 00:20:32.861
Oh. it's just some freak optical effect.
I'm bored already.

296
00:20:34.408 --> 00:20:38.570
Passenger selected.
Pursuit engaged.

297
00:20:45.246 --> 00:20:47.046
WATER RUNS

298
00:20:53.415 --> 00:20:54.489
Hey!

299
00:20:54.555 --> 00:20:56.850
- SHE KNOCKS
- I'll make you a cuppa for the bath.

300
00:21:07.325 --> 00:21:08.565
PHONE RINGS

301
00:21:12.764 --> 00:21:13.800
Hey.

302
00:21:13.990 --> 00:21:15.553
Sorry I'm not there. love.

303
00:21:15.678 --> 00:21:18.537
but I think we both know
it's time I treated myself.

304
00:21:18.811 --> 00:21:20.155
Are you with Neville?

305
00:21:20.233 --> 00:21:23.489
Why would I be back with
Neville after last time?

306
00:21:23.662 --> 00:21:26.022
Why do you think I'm such an idiot?

307
00:21:26.272 --> 00:21:28.131
Well. you're calling from his phone.

308
00:21:30.670 --> 00:21:33.194
Is there someone staying
here in the flat?

309
00:21:33.405 --> 00:21:35.522
Of course not. no. What
are you talking about?

310
00:21:36.755 --> 00:21:40.381
Er... nothing. never mind.
I'll see you tomorrow.

311
00:21:52.419 --> 00:21:54.154
GENTLE SPLASHING

312
00:21:57.315 --> 00:21:58.915
Hello?

313
00:22:01.603 --> 00:22:02.649
Is someone in there?

314
00:22:02.766 --> 00:22:04.391
WATER SPLASHES

315
00:22:04.791 --> 00:22:06.449
Is that Barry?

316
00:22:06.744 --> 00:22:09.259
Because she's with Neville.
and it's not my fault.

317
00:22:11.250 --> 00:22:13.650
WET FOOTSTEPS APPROACH

318
00:22:19.024 --> 00:22:21.395
Sorry. I need to know who's in there.

319
00:22:23.840 --> 00:22:25.551
I'm coming in.

320
00:22:25.729 --> 00:22:27.223
Do you hear me?

321
00:22:30.589 --> 00:22:32.789
Make yourself... decent.

322
00:22:57.490 --> 00:23:01.013
If that's Barry. let's not make
this worse. Just say it's you.

323
00:23:28.530 --> 00:23:29.842
BILL SCREAMS

324
00:23:43.055 --> 00:23:44.495
Hey!

325
00:23:49.267 --> 00:23:50.477
BILL PANTS HEAVILY

326
00:23:55.250 --> 00:23:56.730
LIQUID TRICKLES

327
00:24:26.295 --> 00:24:27.969
Hello.

328
00:24:28.063 --> 00:24:29.223
Hello.

329
00:24:35.414 --> 00:24:36.853
You scared me.

330
00:24:37.025 --> 00:24:38.265
You scared me.

331
00:25:12.027 --> 00:25:13.529
You're dead.

332
00:25:13.639 --> 00:25:15.439
You're dead.

333
00:25:20.891 --> 00:25:22.101
DOOR OPENS

334
00:25:29.392 --> 00:25:32.009
- LIQUID GUSHES
- Hello. Bill.

335
00:25:32.439 --> 00:25:33.999
Oh!

336
00:25:37.770 --> 00:25:39.490
What's that?

337
00:25:47.032 --> 00:25:48.865
I'll tell you what it isn't.

338
00:25:48.970 --> 00:25:51.126
It isn't a freak optical effect...

339
00:26:00.266 --> 00:26:02.188
..and it's following me.

340
00:26:02.951 --> 00:26:04.579
BILL WHIMPERS

341
00:26:09.789 --> 00:26:11.669
No. no. what are you doing?

342
00:26:12.810 --> 00:26:15.929
I'll tell you what. let's
just pop into my box.

343
00:26:16.328 --> 00:26:19.320
Your box? What good is getting
in your box going to do?

344
00:26:19.469 --> 00:26:22.492
What an extraordinarily long and
involved answer this is going to be.

345
00:26:25.320 --> 00:26:27.409
How do we stop it getting in?
We're trapped in here!

346
00:26:27.485 --> 00:26:29.409
Nothing gets through these doors.

347
00:26:29.539 --> 00:26:31.258
They're made of wood.

348
00:26:31.461 --> 00:26:33.344
They've got windows!

349
00:26:38.297 --> 00:26:40.617
Look. this is all mad. I know.

350
00:26:40.711 --> 00:26:44.125
But that's the girl I
told you about Heather...

351
00:26:45.141 --> 00:26:48.024
..only I don't think it's really her.

352
00:26:49.386 --> 00:26:50.813
I know this is hard to believe.

353
00:26:50.930 --> 00:26:54.039
I know you're not exactly
a sci-fi person...

354
00:26:57.328 --> 00:26:59.890
Time and Relative Dimension in Space.

355
00:27:02.543 --> 00:27:04.783
TARDIS for short.

356
00:27:07.797 --> 00:27:09.477
You're safe in here.

357
00:27:09.730 --> 00:27:12.141
You're safe in here and
you always will be.

358
00:27:19.047 --> 00:27:20.610
Any questions?

359
00:27:24.235 --> 00:27:26.035
Is this a knock-through?

360
00:27:27.123 --> 00:27:28.609
Well. in a way. yes.

361
00:27:31.171 --> 00:27:32.726
Look at this place.

362
00:27:34.624 --> 00:27:35.939
- It's like a...
- ..spaceship.

363
00:27:35.984 --> 00:27:37.291
..kitchen.

364
00:27:37.346 --> 00:27:39.937
- A what?
- A really posh kitchen. all metal.

365
00:27:39.968 --> 00:27:42.655
What happened with the doors. though?
Did you run out of money?

366
00:27:43.030 --> 00:27:47.249
What you are standing in
is a technological marvel.

367
00:27:47.534 --> 00:27:50.257
It is science beyond magic.

368
00:27:51.593 --> 00:27:56.476
This is the gateway to everything
that ever was... or ever can be.

369
00:27:58.843 --> 00:28:00.577
Can I use the toilet?

370
00:28:01.780 --> 00:28:04.562
- Pardon?
- I've had a fright.

371
00:28:04.937 --> 00:28:06.053
I need the toilet.

372
00:28:06.155 --> 00:28:09.929
It's down there. first right. second
left. past the macaroon dispenser.

373
00:28:10.007 --> 00:28:11.062
Thanks.

374
00:28:11.132 --> 00:28:15.124
Oh. human! Human alert.
Doyou want me to repel her?

375
00:28:15.195 --> 00:28:17.398
She's just passing through.
She wants to use the toilet.

376
00:28:17.538 --> 00:28:19.649
Oh. I'd give it a minute if I were you.

377
00:28:19.728 --> 00:28:21.900
- THUD!
- Oh. what was that?

378
00:28:22.017 --> 00:28:25.072
We have an incursion on campus.
Extra-terrestrial.

379
00:28:25.177 --> 00:28:26.674
We're under attack.

380
00:28:28.087 --> 00:28:29.607
Let's move.

381
00:28:31.734 --> 00:28:34.890
Oh. my God! This isn't
just a room. is it?

382
00:28:34.968 --> 00:28:36.726
No. it's not just a room.

383
00:28:36.913 --> 00:28:38.366
This is a lift!

384
00:28:43.982 --> 00:28:45.662
Well. come on. then.

385
00:28:57.312 --> 00:29:00.570
No interference here. as far as
I can see. The vault's secure.

386
00:29:02.311 --> 00:29:04.162
So your box can move?

387
00:29:05.060 --> 00:29:06.732
It can go anywhere it likes?

388
00:29:06.896 --> 00:29:08.849
Mm. Good. isn't it?

389
00:29:09.005 --> 00:29:10.873
Anywhere at all. in
the whole university?

390
00:29:10.970 --> 00:29:14.802
Is it my imagination. or is
this taking longer than normal?

391
00:29:17.068 --> 00:29:18.584
Hang on.

392
00:29:19.490 --> 00:29:21.755
The room's still inside the box.

393
00:29:22.279 --> 00:29:24.568
- This isn't a knock-through.
- Nope.

394
00:29:24.685 --> 00:29:27.763
Doctor! It's bigger on the inside
than it is on the outside!

395
00:29:27.849 --> 00:29:29.927
Wey-hey! We got there!

396
00:29:31.701 --> 00:29:34.396
How is that possible?
How do you do that?

397
00:29:34.802 --> 00:29:38.607
Well. first. you have to
imagine a very big box

398
00:29:38.740 --> 00:29:41.099
fitting inside a very small box.

399
00:29:41.250 --> 00:29:44.685
- OK.
- Then you have to make one.

400
00:29:45.037 --> 00:29:47.009
It's the second part people
normally get stuck on.

401
00:29:47.138 --> 00:29:48.969
Can we shut up. please? Busy. busy.

402
00:29:49.060 --> 00:29:51.240
I need to know if there's any
interest in what's inside

403
00:29:51.326 --> 00:29:53.809
- this vault.
- Why. what's inside it?

404
00:29:53.935 --> 00:29:56.341
Something I don't want anyone
being too curious about.

405
00:29:56.529 --> 00:29:58.365
So you put it in the
middle of a university?

406
00:29:58.498 --> 00:30:02.224
Ooh. valid point. Yeah. nice.

407
00:30:02.599 --> 00:30:05.169
Either the creature came here
specifically for what's in here.

408
00:30:05.255 --> 00:30:07.825
- or it's just a coincidence.
- It's just a coincidence.

409
00:30:08.091 --> 00:30:09.818
Well. we can't know that for sure.

410
00:30:09.935 --> 00:30:13.396
Yeah. we can. It was here for
ages before it did anything.

411
00:30:13.482 --> 00:30:15.849
If it had work to do. why would
it lie around in a puddle?

412
00:30:15.920 --> 00:30:19.646
- I don't know. maybe it's a student.
- Oh. banter.

413
00:30:19.787 --> 00:30:21.209
It's good. this.

414
00:30:22.189 --> 00:30:23.348
Your go again.

415
00:30:23.404 --> 00:30:25.684
LIQUID GUSHES

416
00:30:30.975 --> 00:30:32.575
Nardole...

417
00:30:34.613 --> 00:30:38.995
..we need to move away from the
doors and towards the TARDIS.

418
00:30:52.702 --> 00:30:54.874
LIQUID TRICKLES

419
00:31:13.138 --> 00:31:14.873
What if it attacks us?

420
00:31:17.155 --> 00:31:19.034
Well. that's good news.

421
00:31:19.343 --> 00:31:21.867
It means it's not interested
in what's inside the vault.

422
00:31:22.085 --> 00:31:23.828
It just wants to kill us.

423
00:31:24.125 --> 00:31:25.394
Oh.

424
00:31:31.068 --> 00:31:32.489
Run!

425
00:31:33.849 --> 00:31:36.763
It's not interested in the
vault. it's chasing us.

426
00:31:37.138 --> 00:31:38.489
Let's give it a proper challenge.

427
00:31:38.622 --> 00:31:41.278
let's see how far she's prepared to go.

428
00:31:41.339 --> 00:31:44.895
But what about my friend. what
about Heather? Can you save her?

429
00:31:46.061 --> 00:31:49.021
First things first. Let's
see if we can survive her.

430
00:31:53.904 --> 00:31:55.733
SEAGULLS CALL

431
00:32:12.225 --> 00:32:13.569
But...

432
00:32:13.640 --> 00:32:14.889
Yes.

433
00:32:14.975 --> 00:32:16.855
- ..we've moved again.
- We have.

434
00:32:18.342 --> 00:32:19.882
- It was night.
- Yep.

435
00:32:20.280 --> 00:32:23.444
Now it's... day.

436
00:32:23.968 --> 00:32:25.405
Definitely day.

437
00:32:25.655 --> 00:32:27.686
Oh. my God!
Have we travelled in time?

438
00:32:27.749 --> 00:32:31.257
No. of course not.
We've travelled to Australia.

439
00:32:43.597 --> 00:32:46.175
- How are you doing?
- How do you think?

440
00:32:51.458 --> 00:32:53.003
Right. um...

441
00:32:55.121 --> 00:32:56.458
How do I help?

442
00:32:57.333 --> 00:32:59.329
- Can I ask you a personal question?
- No.

443
00:32:59.427 --> 00:33:02.009
- Can I anyway?
- Yes.

444
00:33:02.200 --> 00:33:03.427
Are you from space?

445
00:33:03.530 --> 00:33:05.529
No. of course not.

446
00:33:05.935 --> 00:33:07.409
Nobody's from space.

447
00:33:07.669 --> 00:33:09.489
I'm from a planet
like everybody else.

448
00:33:09.646 --> 00:33:11.406
This planet?

449
00:33:12.435 --> 00:33:15.778
- No. not specifically this one.
- Doesn't make sense. then.

450
00:33:16.810 --> 00:33:17.894
What doesn't?

451
00:33:18.004 --> 00:33:20.457
TARDIS. If you're from another
planet.

452
00:33:20.542 --> 00:33:22.121
why would you name
your box in English?

453
00:33:22.246 --> 00:33:24.457
Those initials wouldn't
work in any other language!

454
00:33:24.551 --> 00:33:27.231
- People don't generally bring that up.
- It looks like a phone box.

455
00:33:27.262 --> 00:33:31.129
Yes. well. that's the cloaking device.
It sort of hides itself.

456
00:33:31.340 --> 00:33:33.957
It's hidden itself as a box with
"pull to enter" on the front?

457
00:33:34.004 --> 00:33:37.949
Uh-huh. It's stuck. It's supposed
to blend in. but it's broken.

458
00:33:41.210 --> 00:33:43.014
GURGLING FROM SINK

459
00:33:48.275 --> 00:33:49.755
Doctor...

460
00:33:50.592 --> 00:33:53.623
Out. out. everybody out. shark attack!

461
00:33:55.182 --> 00:33:57.146
HEATHER SCREAMS

462
00:33:59.346 --> 00:34:00.386
Where are we going?

463
00:34:00.439 --> 00:34:03.268
As far as we can. She made
Australia in a minute

464
00:34:03.408 --> 00:34:04.728
let's see what she can really do.

465
00:34:04.807 --> 00:34:07.252
Sir. we're leaving Earth.
What about the vault?

466
00:34:07.361 --> 00:34:08.634
Oh. we're fine.

467
00:34:08.680 --> 00:34:10.766
If there's any trouble.
I'll get a message on this.

468
00:34:10.791 --> 00:34:13.127
Let's see how long it
takes her to get here.

469
00:34:13.639 --> 00:34:14.919
Where are we?

470
00:34:16.079 --> 00:34:17.853
Other end of the universe.

471
00:34:18.931 --> 00:34:24.417
23 million years in the future.

472
00:34:26.691 --> 00:34:29.331
Oh. yes. it's a time machine too.

473
00:34:52.248 --> 00:34:55.129
So this is... somewhere else?

474
00:34:55.287 --> 00:34:56.849
This is a different planet?

475
00:34:57.044 --> 00:34:58.700
Not Earth. a different one?

476
00:34:58.993 --> 00:35:00.713
That's the general idea.

477
00:35:04.098 --> 00:35:06.649
That's different sky? Is it
made of something different?

478
00:35:06.755 --> 00:35:08.426
- What is sky made of?
- Lemon drops.

479
00:35:08.497 --> 00:35:09.534
Really?

480
00:35:09.559 --> 00:35:11.089
No. but wouldn't that be nice?

481
00:35:11.161 --> 00:35:13.966
You can be very silly
sometimes. do you know that?

482
00:35:14.309 --> 00:35:18.497
So how do we know this... water
thing is actually dangerous?

483
00:35:18.661 --> 00:35:20.442
Ah. because most things are.

484
00:35:20.591 --> 00:35:22.848
- Mm. that's true.
- Why? Is everything out here evil?

485
00:35:22.919 --> 00:35:26.317
Hardly anything is evil. but
most things are hungry.

486
00:35:26.442 --> 00:35:28.746
Hunger looks very like evil from
the wrong end of the cutlery.

487
00:35:28.770 --> 00:35:31.418
Or do you think that your bacon
sandwich loves you back?

488
00:35:31.731 --> 00:35:34.966
So what is it and what
was it doing on Earth?

489
00:35:35.317 --> 00:35:38.294
Well. there were scorch marks on
the concrete where we found it.

490
00:35:38.614 --> 00:35:40.997
Could have been left
by a shuttle craft.

491
00:35:41.833 --> 00:35:43.567
The puddle. what did it look like?

492
00:35:43.650 --> 00:35:45.895
If that was a car. what
would you say that was?

493
00:35:47.161 --> 00:35:48.505
An oil leak?

494
00:35:49.169 --> 00:35:51.145
So it's space engine oil?

495
00:35:51.364 --> 00:35:54.051
Intelligent oil. Super
intelligent space oil.

496
00:35:54.130 --> 00:35:57.348
No. part of the ship itself.
Shape-shifting fluid that becomes

497
00:35:57.418 --> 00:35:58.887
anything it needs to be.

498
00:35:59.490 --> 00:36:00.692
Seriously?

499
00:36:00.770 --> 00:36:03.551
But it spent ages laying around.
being a puddle. what changed?

500
00:36:03.661 --> 00:36:04.942
Your friend.

501
00:36:05.653 --> 00:36:07.934
She looked into it. didn't she?
More than once.

502
00:36:08.418 --> 00:36:09.559
So?

503
00:36:09.692 --> 00:36:11.597
Maybe it saw something it needed.

504
00:36:11.637 --> 00:36:13.239
What was she like. your friend?

505
00:36:13.356 --> 00:36:16.005
What did she want? What did she need?

506
00:36:16.658 --> 00:36:18.818
Everywhere I go. I just want to leave.

507
00:36:22.246 --> 00:36:24.058
I think she wanted to leave.

508
00:36:24.383 --> 00:36:25.583
You see?

509
00:36:26.575 --> 00:36:28.637
The puddle found a passenger.

510
00:36:28.801 --> 00:36:32.692
A left-behind droplet
of a liquid spaceship.

511
00:36:32.871 --> 00:36:36.059
A single tear drop. alone
in a strange world.

512
00:36:36.278 --> 00:36:40.067
Then. one day. it finds someone
who wants to fly away.

513
00:36:40.129 --> 00:36:41.371
Not just a passenger.

514
00:36:41.450 --> 00:36:45.426
more than a passenger it found
a pilot. so it ate her.

515
00:36:46.785 --> 00:36:50.598
- So why is it chasing this one?
- Everything wants. everything needs.

516
00:36:50.809 --> 00:36:52.231
But why does it want her?

517
00:36:52.317 --> 00:36:54.801
I don't know. I don't
know everything. Nardole.

518
00:36:54.903 --> 00:36:57.649
- I don't have it all written down.
- You act like you do.

519
00:36:57.911 --> 00:37:01.833
- I act like I do. because I don't.
- It must be looking for something.

520
00:37:01.989 --> 00:37:04.513
- Of course it is. everything is.
- But what?

521
00:37:04.668 --> 00:37:08.216
What. in the end are
any of us looking for?

522
00:37:08.388 --> 00:37:11.568
We're looking for someone
who's looking for us.

523
00:37:13.370 --> 00:37:15.768
Hey. still making eyes at a puddle?

524
00:37:18.850 --> 00:37:20.610
- HEATHER SCREAMS
- Bill!

525
00:37:22.121 --> 00:37:23.441
Bill!

526
00:37:24.090 --> 00:37:25.569
Quick!

527
00:37:25.570 --> 00:37:27.010
Back to the TARDIS!

528
00:37:33.181 --> 00:37:38.131
OK. it's fast. It time
travels. it never gives up.

529
00:37:39.361 --> 00:37:42.002
Plan! Basic sterilisation.

530
00:37:42.074 --> 00:37:44.357
We're going to run that thing
through the deadliest fire

531
00:37:44.381 --> 00:37:47.098
- in the universe.
- Yes. that sounds excellent.

532
00:37:47.137 --> 00:37:50.286
The deadliest fire in the universe.
That's definitely good.

533
00:37:50.325 --> 00:37:51.434
How do we do that?

534
00:37:51.459 --> 00:37:53.302
The only way we can. We
run through it first.

535
00:37:53.382 --> 00:37:54.825
Less good now.

536
00:37:56.727 --> 00:38:00.055
No. not there. I don't like it there!

537
00:38:02.425 --> 00:38:04.905
- Nardole!
- I don't like there.

538
00:38:07.301 --> 00:38:09.934
I want you running interference.
Can you do that?

539
00:38:10.075 --> 00:38:11.590
- Can I say no. sir?
- No.

540
00:38:11.645 --> 00:38:13.012
- Yes. then.
- Thank you.

541
00:38:13.059 --> 00:38:15.098
- But no really.
- Where are we?

542
00:38:15.170 --> 00:38:17.289
Well. we're basically
in the middle of a war.

543
00:38:17.356 --> 00:38:21.707
No... Well. it's a war zone. and
this is just your basic skirmish.

544
00:38:21.793 --> 00:38:24.051
and it's not as bad as it
sounds. I promise you.

545
00:38:24.168 --> 00:38:27.121
Come on. I've got friends
here. old friends.

546
00:38:27.168 --> 00:38:28.268
Oh...

547
00:38:28.293 --> 00:38:29.569
I say friends...

548
00:38:29.570 --> 00:38:32.649
The Doctor is detected.

549
00:38:32.755 --> 00:38:34.319
Seek. Locate.

550
00:38:34.379 --> 00:38:36.209
- NARDOLE GROANS
- Destroy.

551
00:38:38.397 --> 00:38:42.061
- Are we still in the future?
- No. This is the past.

552
00:38:42.186 --> 00:38:44.570
Doesn't... look like the past.

553
00:38:46.069 --> 00:38:47.458
Are we safe here?

554
00:38:47.483 --> 00:38:49.952
Well. that's up to
Nardole. so probably not.

555
00:38:51.570 --> 00:38:54.319
Oh! Oh. I don't....

556
00:38:54.726 --> 00:38:56.963
Oh! Oh. I don't...

557
00:38:57.090 --> 00:38:59.323
- Keep moving. Doctor!
- Where are we going?

558
00:38:59.416 --> 00:39:00.791
Into the fire. come on.

559
00:39:00.860 --> 00:39:03.034
DISTANT SCREAMING

560
00:39:12.138 --> 00:39:13.738
Who are those guys?

561
00:39:15.850 --> 00:39:18.982
Never mind them. it's
who they're firing at.

562
00:39:31.570 --> 00:39:32.970
Come on.

563
00:39:36.410 --> 00:39:38.913
- What's that?
- The deadliest fire in the universe.

564
00:39:39.084 --> 00:39:43.053
Identify intruder. Identify.

565
00:39:43.405 --> 00:39:45.155
Scan this device and identify me!

566
00:39:45.249 --> 00:39:48.460
You are the Doctor.
You are an enemy of the Daleks!

567
00:39:48.569 --> 00:39:50.850
- Oh. yes. I am!
- Exterminate!

568
00:39:53.388 --> 00:39:54.929
Exterminate.

569
00:39:55.242 --> 00:39:56.810
Exterminate!

570
00:39:58.498 --> 00:40:00.138
Exterminate.

571
00:40:02.219 --> 00:40:05.204
- Exterminate!
- NARDOLE SCREAMS

572
00:40:09.090 --> 00:40:10.996
- What was that thing?
- A Dalek.

573
00:40:11.058 --> 00:40:12.668
- A what?
- A Dalek.

574
00:40:12.706 --> 00:40:15.902
- What's a Dalek?
- Never mind. it's a Dalek.

575
00:40:16.810 --> 00:40:18.660
Exterminate!

576
00:40:25.650 --> 00:40:28.681
Exterminate...

577
00:40:28.954 --> 00:40:33.407
That's wrong. I know my
Daleks. and that's wrong.

578
00:40:36.876 --> 00:40:38.556
Oh. I see.

579
00:40:39.110 --> 00:40:40.289
You see what?

580
00:40:40.439 --> 00:40:42.860
I've sealed the area. all the
Daleks are quarantined...

581
00:40:42.970 --> 00:40:44.267
except that one.

582
00:40:44.681 --> 00:40:46.089
It's OK. This isn't a Dalek.

583
00:40:46.090 --> 00:40:47.541
Look.

584
00:40:48.565 --> 00:40:50.001
Look at the eye.

585
00:40:50.621 --> 00:40:52.119
Heather.

586
00:41:10.452 --> 00:41:11.491
Heather.

587
00:41:11.555 --> 00:41:15.071
Interesting. you had a gun
but you didn't use it. Why?

588
00:41:15.454 --> 00:41:17.798
You've already taken one
person from the Earth.

589
00:41:18.009 --> 00:41:20.329
I'm going to let that
pass. because I have to.

590
00:41:20.490 --> 00:41:23.392
but I will not let you take another.

591
00:41:24.651 --> 00:41:26.051
Go.

592
00:41:27.995 --> 00:41:30.503
Just go. now. Fly away.

593
00:41:35.897 --> 00:41:37.662
Why won't you just go?

594
00:41:45.168 --> 00:41:46.649
Promise you won't go?

595
00:41:46.828 --> 00:41:48.108
Promise.

596
00:41:49.457 --> 00:41:52.754
Oh. my God. I understand.

597
00:41:53.043 --> 00:41:55.051
- You what?
- The last thing she said to me.

598
00:41:55.121 --> 00:41:57.113
She promised she wouldn't
leave without me.

599
00:41:57.324 --> 00:42:00.887
Her last conscious thought.
driving her across the universe.

600
00:42:01.042 --> 00:42:02.705
Never underestimate a crush.

601
00:42:02.816 --> 00:42:04.738
Oh. you don't have to tell me!

602
00:42:05.145 --> 00:42:06.480
What do we do?

603
00:42:06.957 --> 00:42:08.316
I don't know.

604
00:42:08.895 --> 00:42:12.566
She's not chasing you.
she's inviting you.

605
00:42:13.113 --> 00:42:14.215
Release her.

606
00:42:14.801 --> 00:42:17.191
Release her from her promise.

607
00:42:27.221 --> 00:42:28.971
You have to let me go.

608
00:42:29.380 --> 00:42:31.307
You have to let me go.

609
00:42:32.385 --> 00:42:33.659
I will.

610
00:42:33.886 --> 00:42:35.126
I will.

611
00:42:42.490 --> 00:42:44.427
I really liked you.

612
00:42:44.876 --> 00:42:46.716
I really liked you.

613
00:42:55.782 --> 00:42:57.220
Bill...

614
00:42:58.407 --> 00:43:00.071
..don't. don't!

615
00:43:00.236 --> 00:43:01.595
Don't do that!

616
00:43:01.770 --> 00:43:04.681
Listen. please. just listen to him.

617
00:43:08.007 --> 00:43:10.010
Don't. don't! Bill. let go!

618
00:43:12.163 --> 00:43:13.882
Bill. listen to me.

619
00:43:13.980 --> 00:43:16.679
Whatever she's showing you.
whatever she's letting you see.

620
00:43:16.897 --> 00:43:19.546
It's a lure. it's a trap.

621
00:43:19.749 --> 00:43:23.632
She's making you part of her.
and you can never come back.

622
00:43:23.826 --> 00:43:25.655
I see what you see.

623
00:43:28.050 --> 00:43:29.749
It's beautiful.

624
00:43:29.916 --> 00:43:32.257
Bill. let go! You have to let go!

625
00:43:32.660 --> 00:43:35.530
She is not human any more.

626
00:43:37.377 --> 00:43:39.046
Goodbye. Heather.

627
00:43:41.624 --> 00:43:44.564
Goodbye... Bill.

628
00:43:49.241 --> 00:43:50.721
Bill!

629
00:43:59.971 --> 00:44:01.531
You all right?

630
00:44:03.191 --> 00:44:05.183
Yeah. I think so.

631
00:44:13.490 --> 00:44:15.029
You don't look all right.

632
00:44:15.277 --> 00:44:16.740
She's fine.

633
00:44:17.966 --> 00:44:22.622
That's the Doctor for you.
Never notices the tears.

634
00:44:30.295 --> 00:44:32.495
I don't think they're mine.

635
00:44:41.223 --> 00:44:43.285
The vault alarm went
off. but it was nothing.

636
00:44:43.347 --> 00:44:47.473
A student was sick outside and it
registered as a biological attack.

637
00:44:49.290 --> 00:44:51.348
I saw it all for a moment...

638
00:44:52.386 --> 00:44:53.880
..everything out there.

639
00:44:53.996 --> 00:44:56.825
She was going to let me fly with her.
She was inviting me.

640
00:44:57.215 --> 00:44:59.637
- But I was too scared.
- Scared is good.

641
00:45:00.362 --> 00:45:03.521
Scared is rational. She
wasn't human any more.

642
00:45:03.858 --> 00:45:05.378
Will we see her again?

643
00:45:07.283 --> 00:45:08.803
I don't see how.

644
00:45:14.895 --> 00:45:17.605
No. no. no. No. no. You
have to forget about that.

645
00:45:17.809 --> 00:45:19.246
I don't see how I can.

646
00:45:20.315 --> 00:45:21.875
I do.

647
00:45:24.437 --> 00:45:25.637
Come here. Bill.

648
00:45:27.866 --> 00:45:29.249
What's up?

649
00:45:30.132 --> 00:45:32.780
- I just want to fix something.
- Whoa. what are you doing?

650
00:45:32.960 --> 00:45:35.437
- Don't worry. This won't hurt at all.
- No. but tell me.

651
00:45:35.671 --> 00:45:36.888
Nothing.

652
00:45:37.225 --> 00:45:40.005
Yeah. cos I think you're
going to wipe my memory.

653
00:45:41.295 --> 00:45:43.045
I'm not stupid. you know.

654
00:45:43.318 --> 00:45:44.673
That's the trouble with you.

655
00:45:44.708 --> 00:45:46.046
You don't think anyone's
ever seen a movie.

656
00:45:46.070 --> 00:45:48.678
- I know what a mind-wipe looks like!
- I have no choice.

657
00:45:48.748 --> 00:45:51.248
I'm here for a reason.
I'm in disguise.

658
00:45:51.334 --> 00:45:53.089
I have promises to keep.

659
00:45:53.293 --> 00:45:55.824
No-one can know about me.

660
00:45:55.926 --> 00:45:57.289
This is the most exciting thing

661
00:45:57.290 --> 00:46:00.329
that's ever happened to me in my life.
The only exciting thing!

662
00:46:00.330 --> 00:46:01.730
I'm sorry.

663
00:46:03.092 --> 00:46:06.600
OK. Let me remember just for a week.
Just a week.

664
00:46:07.084 --> 00:46:09.615
OK. well. just for tonight.
Just one night.

665
00:46:09.701 --> 00:46:12.010
Come on. let me have some
good dreams for once.

666
00:46:15.985 --> 00:46:17.305
OK.

667
00:46:19.624 --> 00:46:21.504
Do what you've got to do.

668
00:46:23.858 --> 00:46:25.108
But imagine...

669
00:46:26.326 --> 00:46:29.912
..just imagine how it would feel
if someone did this to you.

670
00:46:45.269 --> 00:46:47.136
- Get out!
- What?

671
00:46:47.238 --> 00:46:50.207
You can keep your memories. Now
get out before I change my mind!

672
00:46:50.386 --> 00:46:54.050
Don't speak. don't start. just run!
Now. Go!

673
00:47:01.924 --> 00:47:03.244
Shut up.

674
00:47:03.362 --> 00:47:04.729
You shut up as well.

675
00:47:04.807 --> 00:47:07.213
METALLIC THRUMMING

676
00:47:07.571 --> 00:47:10.196
Will you all please
just leave me alone?

677
00:47:10.282 --> 00:47:12.565
I can't do that any more.
I promised!

678
00:47:39.100 --> 00:47:43.671
It's a big universe. but maybe
one day we'll find her.

679
00:47:53.076 --> 00:47:54.796
What changed your mind?

680
00:47:59.792 --> 00:48:01.072
Time...

681
00:48:02.981 --> 00:48:04.701
Time?

682
00:48:06.624 --> 00:48:08.944
..And Relative Dimension In Space.

683
00:48:20.243 --> 00:48:21.602
It means...

684
00:48:22.521 --> 00:48:24.501
what the hell?!

685
00:48:35.011 --> 00:48:37.010
This is one of Earth's first colonies.

686
00:48:37.090 --> 00:48:40.118
- What are they? Alien birds?
- Tiny robots.

687
00:48:40.180 --> 00:48:43.089
That is a robot. It speaks emoji!

688
00:48:43.384 --> 00:48:44.729
And where are all the people?

689
00:48:44.961 --> 00:48:46.065
Argh!

690
00:48:46.110 --> 00:48:47.142
What. you're going back in?

691
00:48:47.166 --> 00:48:49.899
I'm having this really childish
impulse to blow it up.

692
00:48:54.485 --> 00:48:56.325
- You're the one who should be afraid.
- Never.

693
00:48:56.430 --> 00:48:57.889
Get ready.

694
00:48:58.063 --> 00:48:59.641
HE SCREAMS

695
00:48:59.758 --> 00:49:00.936
I'm the Doctor.

696
00:49:01.352 --> 00:49:02.767
I've been standing
by the gates of

697
00:49:02.815 --> 00:49:05.016
your world. keeping you all safe.

698
00:49:05.259 --> 00:49:07.665
I'm not stopping now. Any questions?

698
00:49:08.305 --> 00:50:08.552
